  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="4ab34dd0-2fba-587f-9538-64b69510c2e0" activityNameId="d8d7dc66-5968-5d9f-9b8b-8e7595ae1997" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, ventilation system, various components, m3/h</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, ventilation system, various components, m3/h
Disposal of various components for a ventilation system with a nominal air flow rate of 5'000-20'000 m3/h at the air handling unit. Reference value of inventory is 1 m3/h nominal air flow of the air handling unit (at 2 m/s air speed in cross section of air filter or heat exchanger). The inventory is based on average data of 4 office buildings, 3 schools and 3 residential care homes with a total heated gross floor area of 61719 m2 and a total nominal air flow of 302190 m3/h, specific weight of the components: 0.17 kg/(m3/h), including average components for air valves, air intake, roof-hoods, dampers, fire dampers, silencers and sensors. The data represent a ventilation system mainly made of galvanized steel.
Transport to dismantling facilities, machines for handling in sorting plant, electricity demand for sorting plant, final disposal of waste material. Cut-off to recycling for metals.
Location:  Specific to the technology mix encountered in sorting plants in Switzerland.
Technology: Disposal to a sorting plant assumed. Metal pieces, copper in cables and electronic devices are recycled, plastic parts are incinerated, inert wastes (e.g. rock wool) are landfilled.
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2013. Disposal technology mix as used in late 1990ies
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Waste-specific calculation based on production input data
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_3fd2478c-39bc-4ede-b7e0-4bf086b14d57.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="fdab769f-4bdb-5024-8349-c1745bbb2597" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">CH</shortname>
